          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
      <p><em>Spread is shown from each listed player's own team perspective (negative = favorite). Implied team total = (Game Total − Team Spread) ÷ 2. "vs." labels the matchup only and doesn't indicate home/away. Injury blank = Active; none of this roster's players currently carry a Questionable/Doubtful/Out tag. Roster floor: ~109.71. Roster ceiling: ~222.23. Full $50,000 cap spent.</em></p>
      <h3>What the Numbers Tell Us</h3>
      <p>Five of nine roster spots touch one of two correlated games — Carolina-Atlanta (Young, Coker, Robinson) and Cincinnati-Houston (Hutchinson, Chase) — while Watson, Goedert, and the Jaguars D/ST stand entirely apart from both. That's a genuinely different shape from Balanced this week: rather than one accidental cluster spreading across the roster, this build has two deliberate, self-contained correlation plays sitting alongside independent value picks. The full $50,000 cap is spent, with Ja'Marr Chase's $7,600 salary the one spot where the build pays for talent rather than hunting for a discount.</p>
      <h3>DFS Translation</h3>
      <p><strong>How to read Grade and Signal:</strong> Signal layers Value (projected points per $1,000 of salary) on top of Grade to flag roster fit:</p>
      <ul class="dfs-list">
        <li><strong>CORE</strong> — Grade A and Value at or above a position-specific bar. Build your lineup around this player.</li>
        <li><strong>VALUE</strong> — Salary at or below a position-specific ceiling and Value at or above a bar. A cheap, efficient pivot that frees up cap space.</li>
        <li><strong>WATCH</strong> — Neither bar was cleared. Not a red flag, just no strong edge either way.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>The exact cutoffs differ by position — a WR needs fewer raw points than a QB to earn a Grade A, for example:</p>
      <div class="roster-wrap">
        <table class="roster-table">
          <thead><tr><th>Position</th><th>Grade A</th><th>Grade B</th><th>CORE — Value &ge;</th><th>VALUE — Salary &le;</th><th>VALUE — Value percentile &ge;</th></tr></thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr><td class="pos">QB</td><td>&ge; 20</td><td>&ge; 16</td><td>2.95</td><td>$6,500</td><td>65th</td></tr>
            <tr><td class="pos">RB</td><td>&ge; 18</td><td>&ge; 12</td><td>2.5</td><td>$5,800</td><td>65th</td></tr>
            <tr><td class="pos">WR</td><td>&ge; 16</td><td>&ge; 11</td><td>2.4</td><td>$5,200</td><td>65th</td></tr>
            <tr><td class="pos">TE</td><td>&ge; 15</td><td>&ge; 10</td><td>2.5</td><td>$3,700</td><td>65th</td></tr>
            <tr><td class="pos">DST</td><td>&ge; 7.5</td><td>top 42% (58th pct)</td><td>2.4</td><td>$2,600</td><td>65th</td></tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
      <p>Below the Grade B line at each position is a Grade C; missing both the CORE and VALUE bars is a WATCH.</p>
      <p>For this build specifically:</p>
      <div class="translation-row">
        <div class="translation-pill core"><b>CORE</b>Bijan Robinson, Christian Watson, Xavier Hutchinson, Dallas Goedert, Jaguars D/ST</div>
        <div class="translation-pill value"><b>VALUE (leverage)</b>Bryce Young, Jalen Coker</div>
        <div class="translation-pill watch"><b>WATCH</b>Ashton Jeanty, Ja'Marr Chase</div>
      </div>
      <p>Five CORE, two VALUE, two WATCH — real ownership differentiation across two self-contained correlation clusters.</p>
      <h3>The Slate-IQ Take</h3>
      <p>The two-cluster structure here is sound and matches what Leverage is supposed to look like — genuine correlation, real ownership differentiation (Hutchinson at $3,500 in particular), without going as far into game-stacking as Ceiling does. The one spot worth a plain-spoken flag is Ja'Marr Chase: Grade A on production, but his value rank (18th among 39 WRs) is a real step down from what this build's other pieces offer, the direct cost of needing a same-tier correlation partner for Hutchinson at a salary that fit. Ashton Jeanty is a strong talent (Grade A) that the model still calls WATCH rather than CORE — worth knowing that's an unproven-workload bet, not a locked-in one.</p>
      <h3>Final Takeaway</h3>
      <p>This build's edge comes from two separate, real correlation plays rather than one big story — Carolina's QB/WR/bring-back stack and the Cincinnati-Houston crossover — with Xavier Hutchinson's $3,500 price tag standing out as the single clearest mispricing on the roster.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ============ GPP #2 ============ -->
<section class="lineup-section" id="gpp2">
  <div class="container">
    <span class="lineup-tag tag-gpp">GPP #2 · Tournament Build</span>
    <h2>Week 2 GPP Lineup: Bears-Vikings Full Bring-Back</h2>
    <p class="lineup-excerpt">A full bring-back build around the Bears-Vikings game — five of nine roster spots tied to one 49.5-point environment, both sides represented.</p>
    <div class="lineup-stats-row">
      <div class="lineup-stat-pill"><span class="v">$50,000</span><span class="l">Salary Used</span></div>
      <div class="lineup-stat-pill"><span class="v">141.34</span><span class="l">Proj. Total</span></div>
      <div class="lineup-stat-pill"><span class="v">5-Man</span><span class="l">Same-Game Stack</span></div>
    </div>
    <div class="article-body">
      <h3>Definition</h3>
      <p><strong>Ceiling is the highest-ceiling, most aggressive-correlation build, willing to sacrifice floor for upside.</strong> It gets 4 of the week's 15 $1 entries, paired one-for-one with a Leverage entry into Three-Entry Max GPPs. Construction-wise it leans hardest into game stacks and volatility — more volatile WRs, lower-owned players, and often a different QB and game environment entirely from the other three builds.</p>
      <h3>Why This Lineup, Why Now</h3>
      <p>This is the most concentrated correlation play of the week's four established builds: 5 of 9 roster spots are tied to the Chicago-Minnesota game — Caleb Williams, D'Andre Swift, and Rome Odunze on the Bears side, Jordan Addison and the Vikings D/ST on the Vikings side. That's a genuine bring-back structure, both offenses represented, built around a 49.5-point total. One accuracy note worth flagging: that 49.5 total is the 2nd-highest on this week's board, not the single highest — Washington-Dallas actually carries the week's top total at 50.5. This roster does touch that game too, through Stefon Diggs, but only as a single-player look rather than a second full stack. The construction logic here is "lean into the best available two-sided game correlation," which this week means Chicago-Minnesota rather than literally the highest number on the slate.</p>
      <h3>The Lineup, Player by Player</h3>
      <p><strong>QB — Caleb Williams ($6,800, CHI vs. MIN)</strong><br>Grade A, WATCH signal, projected for 23.77 points — 1st among 25 active QBs in raw points. The centerpiece of this build's bring-back — Chicago's clear passing-game hub in the week's 2nd-highest total game, for a 27.5 implied team total, with three of his own weapons rostered around him or across the field. Grade A on production; the WATCH tag reflects that his value rank (5th) sits behind several cheaper options, not a concern about the matchup itself.</p>
      <p><strong>RB — D'Andre Swift ($6,300, CHI vs. MIN)</strong><br>Grade A, CORE signal, projected for 20.09 points — 3rd among 35 active RBs in raw points and value. Chicago's clear lead back in a game the team is favored to control (-5.5), for a 27.5 implied team total — a stable floor with real upside if the shootout script materializes.</p>
      <p><strong>RB — Chase Brown ($6,900, CIN vs. HOU)</strong><br>Grade B, WATCH signal, projected for 17.48 points — 6th among RBs in raw points, 9th in value. The one roster spot with no tie to the Chicago-Minnesota correlation — a solid, standalone play in a good CIN@HOU environment (21.75 implied total) on its own merits.</p>
      <p><strong>WR — Rome Odunze ($5,500, CHI vs. MIN)</strong><br>Grade B, WATCH signal, projected for 11.30 points — 22nd among 39 active WRs in raw points and value. The more speculative half of the Bears' side of the bring-back — behind Williams and Swift in expected usage, but here to complete the game correlation rather than on a standout individual case, for a 27.5 implied team total.</p>
      <p><strong>WR — Stefon Diggs ($5,300, WAS vs. DAL)</strong><br>Grade B, WATCH signal, projected for 13.81 points — 10th among WRs in raw points, 8th in value. The lineup's one look at the actual highest total on the board (50.5, Washington-Dallas), for a 23.5 implied team total — a single-player exposure rather than a second full stack.</p>
      <p><strong>WR — Jordan Addison ($5,100, MIN vs. CHI)</strong><br>Grade B, VALUE signal, projected for 13.59 points — 12th among WRs in raw points, 7th in value. The Vikings' side of the bring-back — Minnesota is a 5.5-point underdog in this game, the negative-script role that tends to support receiving volume, for a 22.0 implied team total.</p>
      <p><strong>TE — Trey McBride ($6,900, ARI vs. SEA)</strong><br>Grade A, WATCH signal, projected for 20.46 points — 1st among 27 active TEs in raw points, 5th in value — the most expensive non-RB piece in the lineup and the only Arizona exposure on this roster, entirely outside the Chicago-Minnesota correlation, for an 18.5 implied team total.</p>
      <p><strong>FLEX — Wan'Dale Robinson ($4,600, TEN vs. PHI)</strong><br>Grade B, VALUE signal, projected for 12.84 points — 15th among WRs in raw points, 6th in value. A cheap, standalone salary-efficient piece in the TEN@PHI game (16.25 implied total) — not tied to any other roster spot, here to free up cap for the rest of the build.</p>
      <p><strong>DST — Minnesota Vikings ($2,600, MIN vs. CHI)</strong><br>Grade A, CORE signal, projected for 8.00 points — 4th among 26 active DSTs in raw points, 3rd in value. The final piece of the Chicago-Minnesota bring-back, for a 22.0 implied team total, and a strong unit independent of that tie.</p>
      <h3>The Full Roster</h3>
      <div class="roster-wrap">
        <table class="roster-table">
          <thead><tr><th>Pos</th><th>Player</th><th>Salary</th><th>Matchup</th><th>Vegas (Total/Spread)</th><th>Implied Total</th><th>Proj. DK</th><th>Value ($/1K)</th><th>Grade</th><th>Signal</th></tr></thead>
