</section>

<!-- ============ HYBRID ============ -->
<section class="lineup-section" id="hybrid">
  <div class="container">
    <span class="lineup-tag tag-hybrid">Hybrid · Fifth Build</span>
    <h2>Week 2 Hybrid Lineup: Grade-A Watch List Build</h2>
    <p class="lineup-excerpt">A fifth build this week, forcing in four of the model's Grade-A/WATCH prospects around two proven CORE holdovers — full cap spent, zero cushion left.</p>
    <div class="lineup-stats-row">
      <div class="lineup-stat-pill"><span class="v">$50,000</span><span class="l">Salary Used</span></div>
      <div class="lineup-stat-pill"><span class="v">151.07</span><span class="l">Proj. Total</span></div>
      <div class="lineup-stat-pill"><span class="v">4</span><span class="l">Grade-A/WATCH Bets</span></div>
    </div>
    <div class="article-body">
      <h3>Definition</h3>
      <p><strong>Hybrid isn't one of Slate-IQ's four established weekly archetypes (Cash, Balanced, Leverage, Ceiling) — it's a fifth, standalone build</strong> tied to two specific DK entry IDs outside the normal 2-of-4 exposure-cap system that governs the other four. Per its own construction label in the workbook, the thesis is to force in players the model grades A on raw production but hasn't yet certified with a CORE or VALUE signal — high-conviction talent the numbers like, without the efficiency or proven-workload case a CORE tag requires. This roster hasn't changed since it was first built earlier this week. <strong>Open question:</strong> which contest(s) this goes into and how many entries it gets haven't been specified — that's being treated as unresolved rather than guessed at.</p>
      <h3>Why This Lineup, Why Now</h3>
      <p>Four of the nine roster spots — Caleb Williams, Ashton Jeanty, De'Von Achane, and the Seahawks D/ST — are Grade A players the model still flags WATCH rather than CORE or VALUE, meaning the raw production case is strong but hasn't cleared the efficiency (Value) or price (salary ceiling + percentile) bar that would make them a "safe" build-around. Christian Watson and Derrick Henry anchor the roster as the two genuinely proven CORE holdovers, and Jalen Coker, Wan'Dale Robinson, and Darren Waller round it out as cheap, efficient VALUE plays that free up cap space for the four bigger bets. The full $50,000 is spent — there's no cushion left if any of the four WATCH-tier pieces disappoints.</p>
      <h3>The Lineup, Player by Player</h3>
      <p><strong>QB — Caleb Williams ($6,800, CHI vs. MIN)</strong><br>Grade A, WATCH signal, projected for 23.77 points — 1st among 25 active QBs in raw points. The single highest QB projection on the entire board, for a 27.5 implied team total — Grade A on production, WATCH because his value rank (5th) trails several cheaper options in a week where price-efficient QBs are plentiful.</p>
      <p><strong>RB — Ashton Jeanty ($6,800, LV vs. LAC)</strong><br>Grade A, WATCH signal, projected for 20.05 points — 4th among 35 active RBs in raw points and value. A strong Grade A profile the model hasn't fully certified yet — real talent, unproven workload consistency at this price, for an 18.25 implied team total.</p>
      <p><strong>RB — De'Von Achane ($6,700, MIA vs. SF)</strong><br>Grade A, WATCH signal, projected for 18.34 points — 5th among RBs in raw points and value. Miami is a 13.5-point underdog — the widest spread on the board, for a 16.0 implied team total — which cuts both ways for a receiving-heavy back: more garbage-time targets, but a real risk of the run game getting abandoned early.</p>
      <p><strong>WR — Christian Watson ($6,200, GB vs. NYJ)</strong><br>Grade A, CORE signal, projected for 19.08 points — 3rd among 39 active WRs in raw points and value alike. The same profile that makes him a CORE piece in Leverage — a proven, efficient play rather than a speculative one here, for a 24.0 implied team total.</p>
      <p><strong>WR — Jalen Coker ($5,100, CAR vs. ATL)</strong><br>Grade B, VALUE signal, projected for 15.30 points — 7th among WRs in raw points, 4th in value. A cheap, efficient complement freeing up cap for the four bigger bets elsewhere on this roster, for a 22.5 implied team total.</p>
      <p><strong>WR — Wan'Dale Robinson ($4,600, TEN vs. PHI)</strong><br>Grade B, VALUE signal, projected for 12.84 points — 15th among WRs in raw points, 6th in value. The cheapest WR on the roster and a clean value hold, same role it plays in this week's Ceiling build, for a 16.25 implied team total.</p>
      <p><strong>FLEX — Derrick Henry ($7,200, BAL vs. NO)</strong><br>Grade A, CORE signal, projected for 23.10 points — 2nd among RBs in raw points, 1st in value. The most expensive player in the lineup and the roster's other proven anchor — an 8.5-point favorite with the clearest touchdown equity on the board, for a 28.0 implied team total.</p>
      <p><strong>TE — Darren Waller ($3,100, CAR vs. ATL)</strong><br>Grade C, VALUE signal, projected for 9.52 points — the cheapest player on the roster. Not part of the Grade-A/WATCH thesis — this is straightforward salary relief that also happens to land on the same Carolina game as Jalen Coker (22.5 implied total), freeing up cap for the four bigger bets elsewhere.</p>
      <p><strong>DST — Seattle Seahawks ($3,500, SEA vs. ARI)</strong><br>Grade A, WATCH signal, projected for 9.08 points — 2nd among 26 active DSTs in raw points. A strong unit the model likes on production but hasn't certified on value (6th), for a 23.0 implied team total — the fourth and final Grade-A/WATCH piece in this build.</p>
      <h3>The Full Roster</h3>
      <div class="roster-wrap">
        <table class="roster-table">
          <thead><tr><th>Pos</th><th>Player</th><th>Salary</th><th>Matchup</th><th>Vegas (Total/Spread)</th><th>Implied Total</th><th>Proj. DK</th><th>Value ($/1K)</th><th>Grade</th><th>Signal</th></tr></thead>
          <tbody>
