            <tr><td class="pos">FLEX</td><td class="name">Derrick Henry</td><td>$7,200</td><td>BAL vs. NO</td><td>47.5 / -8.5</td><td>28.0</td><td>23.10</td><td>3.21</td><td class="grade">A</td><td class="signal-CORE">CORE</td></tr>
            <tr><td class="pos">TE</td><td class="name">Darren Waller</td><td>$3,100</td><td>CAR vs. ATL</td><td>43.5 / -1.5</td><td>22.5</td><td>9.52</td><td>3.07</td><td class="grade">C</td><td class="signal-VALUE">VALUE</td></tr>
            <tr><td class="pos">DST</td><td class="name">Seahawks</td><td>$3,500</td><td>SEA vs. ARI</td><td>41.5 / -4.5</td><td>23.0</td><td>9.08</td><td>2.59</td><td class="grade">A</td><td class="signal-WATCH">WATCH</td></tr>
            <tr class="total"><td colspan="2">Total</td><td>$50,000</td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td>151.07</td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
      <p><em>Spread is shown from each listed player's own team perspective (negative = favorite). Implied team total = (Game Total − Team Spread) ÷ 2. "vs." labels the matchup only and doesn't indicate home/away. Injury blank = Active; none of this roster's players currently carry a Questionable/Doubtful/Out tag. Roster floor: ~104.84. Roster ceiling: ~212.40. Full $50,000 cap spent.</em></p>
      <h3>What the Numbers Tell Us</h3>
      <p>The only real correlation here is incidental: Jalen Coker and Darren Waller both sit on Carolina's side of CAR@ATL, a two-player look that wasn't the point of either pick. Otherwise this roster is spread across seven different games, which fits a build that's organized around player conviction (Grade A talent) rather than game environment. The full $50,000 cap being spent, with zero cushion, means every one of the four WATCH-tier bets needs to hold up roughly as projected — there's no cheap floor play elsewhere absorbing the risk if one of them doesn't.</p>
      <h3>DFS Translation</h3>
      <p><strong>How to read Grade and Signal:</strong> Signal layers Value (projected points per $1,000 of salary) on top of Grade to flag roster fit:</p>
      <ul class="dfs-list">
        <li><strong>CORE</strong> — Grade A and Value at or above a position-specific bar. Build your lineup around this player.</li>
        <li><strong>VALUE</strong> — Salary at or below a position-specific ceiling and Value at or above a bar. A cheap, efficient pivot that frees up cap space.</li>
        <li><strong>WATCH</strong> — Neither bar was cleared. Not a red flag, just no strong edge either way.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>The exact cutoffs differ by position — a WR needs fewer raw points than a QB to earn a Grade A, for example:</p>
      <div class="roster-wrap">
        <table class="roster-table">
          <thead><tr><th>Position</th><th>Grade A</th><th>Grade B</th><th>CORE — Value &ge;</th><th>VALUE — Salary &le;</th><th>VALUE — Value percentile &ge;</th></tr></thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr><td class="pos">QB</td><td>&ge; 20</td><td>&ge; 16</td><td>2.95</td><td>$6,500</td><td>65th</td></tr>
            <tr><td class="pos">RB</td><td>&ge; 18</td><td>&ge; 12</td><td>2.5</td><td>$5,800</td><td>65th</td></tr>
            <tr><td class="pos">WR</td><td>&ge; 16</td><td>&ge; 11</td><td>2.4</td><td>$5,200</td><td>65th</td></tr>
            <tr><td class="pos">TE</td><td>&ge; 15</td><td>&ge; 10</td><td>2.5</td><td>$3,700</td><td>65th</td></tr>
            <tr><td class="pos">DST</td><td>&ge; 7.5</td><td>top 42% (58th pct)</td><td>2.4</td><td>$2,600</td><td>65th</td></tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
      <p>Below the Grade B line at each position is a Grade C; missing both the CORE and VALUE bars is a WATCH.</p>
      <p>For this build specifically:</p>
      <div class="translation-row">
        <div class="translation-pill core"><b>CORE</b>Christian Watson, Derrick Henry</div>
        <div class="translation-pill value"><b>VALUE</b>Jalen Coker, Wan'Dale Robinson, Darren Waller</div>
        <div class="translation-pill watch"><b>WATCH</b>Caleb Williams, Ashton Jeanty, De'Von Achane, Seahawks D/ST</div>
      </div>
      <p>Two CORE, three VALUE, four WATCH — the highest WATCH count of any build this week, by design.</p>
      <h3>The Slate-IQ Take</h3>
      <p>This build is exactly what its own label says it is — a bet on talent the model likes but hasn't fully certified, concentrated in four spots (Williams, Jeanty, Achane, Seahawks) rather than spread thin. That's a real, structural difference from the other four builds this week, all of which lean more heavily on CORE or VALUE signals. Worth being direct that De'Von Achane's 13.5-point spread is the single biggest game-script risk on the roster — that's the widest underdog number on the entire board, and a lopsided game can pull his workload down fast regardless of how the matchup-only numbers read.</p>
      <h3>Final Takeaway</h3>
      <p>A talent-forward, fifth-lineup build: this roster bets on upside the model already likes but hasn't fully certified, rather than the safest path to that talent — worth entering with that framing in mind rather than as a fifth "safe" lineup.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

